    "measurementDetails": "Geometry uses alpha \u226532. Head width/center use the upper 60% of the alpha silhouette, filtered for yellow watercolor pigment (R>130, G>100, R-B>35, G-B>15). All endpoint pair equations use equal weight; head width and silhouette height are normalized by 290 and 489 source pixels, with 1a scale fixed at 1.4. X/Y offsets fit endpoint head centers and baselines. Canvas expanded to include ALL nonzero alpha across every frame, including alpha 1\u20137 speckles in 4a.",
    "limitations": [
      "Uniform clip-wide transforms reduce canvas/scale seams but cannot alter authored character proportions, eye/wing poses, or internal drawing drift.",
      "The 2b seated-to-standing drawings change head-to-body proportion; its transform is a best-fit compromise across both incoming and outgoing neighbors.",
      "4a ends in fading smoke and an empty frame; its scale is determined from standing entry, while full-motion bounds determine canvas padding.",
      "Missing states have identity values only as placeholders and must not be treated as calibrated. Re-review after replacing animation frames; sample hashes/counts identify stale calibration."
    ]
